sn11.22:3.3 starts: To whatever extent Sakka announced his name,
sn35.152:2.12 starts: The mind is suffering …
sn35.152:2.14 starts: Whatever feeling arises with mind-contact as condition
sn36.11:2.9 starts: That has been stated by me with reference to formations
sn36.11:2.10 starts: to formations being subject to vanishing …
an3.40:4.1 starts: For one performing an evil deed
# superseded: an3.40:4.2 none
an3.40:4.3 starts: The self within you knows, O person,
an3.40:6.2 starts: acting unrighteously in the world.
an3.40:6.3 starts: Therefore one should fare mindfully, taking oneself as authority;
